IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpf-self-employed-rates`

-- Central Provident Fund (Self-Employed Persons) Regulations 1992 (Rg 25), regs 2, 2A, 3, 4(1)(m), 7A, 8, 8A, 9A, 13, 14, 16, First
-- Schedule item 23 and Third Schedule, with s 2(1A)(a) of the Act -- worked cases. Expected results written by hand from the
-- deposited text (../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-RG25.txt) and checked twice.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `REQ-0268 (Haziq scenario; Jun Hao scenario, event j043, 2028)`

-- A self-employed delivery rider, born 30 August 2006, declares $31,000 of trade income for a year; the ledger takes him to be
-- 21 and the income not to be platform remuneration. He files in 2028, so the relevant year is taken to be 2027 (INFERENCE: the
-- year the income was earned). On 1 January 2027 he has attained 20 (21 only on 30 August 2027); on 1 January 2028, 21. Either
-- way column (2) of item 23 ("has not attained 35 years of age").
#ASSERT `the age attained on 1 January of the relevant year` 2027 2006 FALSE EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the age attained on 1 January of the relevant year` 2028 2006 FALSE EQUALS 21

-- Taken to be a citizen or permanent resident (reg 2(1)); $31,000 is more than $6,000, so the Regulations apply (reg 3(1)). None
-- of it is platform remuneration, so reg 2A(2) excludes nothing.
#ASSERT `the Regulations apply under regulation 3(1)` TRUE 31000
#ASSERT `the income under regulation 2A(2)` 31000 0 EQUALS 31000

-- THE AMOUNT: income exceeding $18,000, column (2): 8% of 31,000 = 2,480, under the $7,680 maximum. No fraction of a dollar. No
-- estimated contributions under s 9B, so reg 8A deducts nothing.
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 31000 EQUALS 2480
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 21 31000 EQUALS 2480
#ASSERT `the contribution after regulation 8A` 2480 0 EQUALS 2480

-- BY WHEN: "not later than 30 days after the date of issue of the ... contributions notice ... for the relevant year", unless the
-- Board extends it (reg 7A(2)); by instalments if all is paid by then (reg 7A(3)). Day 30 after issue is in time; day 31 is not.
#ASSERT `the last day for paying under regulation 7A(2), in days after the notice` 0 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `paid in time under regulation 7A(2)` 30 0
#ASSERT `paid in time under regulation 7A(2)` 31 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the instalments discharge the contributions under regulation 7A(3)` 2480 2480

§ `s 2(1A)(a) -- age on 1 January`

#ASSERT `the age attained on 1 January of the relevant year` 2027 1992 TRUE EQUALS 35

§ `Reg 3 -- the $6,000 threshold`

#ASSERT `the Regulations apply under regulation 3(1)` TRUE 6000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Regulations apply under regulation 3(1)` TRUE 6001

§ `First Schedule item 23 -- lower band (over $6,000 to $12,000)`

#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 6000 EQUALS 0
-- 4% of 6,001 = 240.04; the fraction is disregarded (reg 14).
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 6001 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 12000 EQUALS 480
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 40 12000 EQUALS 540

§ `First Schedule item 23 -- middle band (over $12,000 to $18,000)`

-- 480 + 0.16 x 3,000 = 960; 540 + 0.18 x 3,000 = 1,080.
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 15000 EQUALS 960
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 40 15000 EQUALS 1080
-- 480 + 0.16 x 345 = 535.20, rounded down to 535.
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 12345 EQUALS 535
-- 480 + 0.16 x 6,000 = 1,440; 8% of 18,001 = 1,440.08, rounded down to 1,440.
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 18000 EQUALS 1440
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 18001 EQUALS 1440

§ `First Schedule item 23 -- top band and the age boundaries`

-- 9% of 31,000 = 2,790; 10.5% = 3,255.
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 34 31000 EQUALS 2480
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 35 31000 EQUALS 2790
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 50 31000 EQUALS 3255
-- On $100,000 each column hits its maximum (8,000 > 7,680; 9,000 > 8,640; 10,500 > 10,080).
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 100000 EQUALS 7680
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 40 100000 EQUALS 8640
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 52 100000 EQUALS 10080

§ `Reg 2A, reg 7A(4A) -- platform remuneration`

#ASSERT `the income under regulation 2A(2)` 31000 31000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the income under regulation 2A(2)` 40000 9000 EQUALS 31000
-- Notice-of-assessment income 31,000 less APE 10,000 = 21,000; 8% of 21,000 = 1,680.
#ASSERT `the income basis under regulation 7A(4A)` 31000 10000 EQUALS 21000
#ASSERT `the regulation 4 contribution` 20 21000 EQUALS 1680

§ `Reg 8A -- estimated contributions`

#ASSERT `the contribution after regulation 8A` 2480 500 EQUALS 1980

§ `Reg 7A(2), (3), reg 16 -- time`

#ASSERT `the last day for paying under regulation 7A(2), in days after the notice` 90 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `paid in time under regulation 7A(2)` 60 90
#ASSERT `the instalments discharge the contributions under regulation 7A(3)` 2000 2480 EQUALS FALSE
-- An objection to the assessment does not by itself postpone payment.
#ASSERT `the time for paying is postponed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Regs 8, 13 -- additional contributions`

#ASSERT `the additional contributions under regulation 8` 2480 2000 EQUALS 480
#ASSERT `the additional contributions under regulation 8` 2480 2479.5 EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 9A, Third Schedule -- the application to reduce`

#ASSERT `the Third Schedule maximum` 2027 20 EQUALS 7680
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule maximum` 2025 20 EQUALS 7104
#ASSERT `the Third Schedule maximum` 2025 52 EQUALS 9324
-- 7,680 - 6,000 = 1,680; already at or over the maximum: nil; well under it: no reduction.
#ASSERT `the contribution after a regulation 9A reduction` 2480 6000 7680 EQUALS 1680
#ASSERT `the contribution after a regulation 9A reduction` 2480 8000 7680 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the contribution after a regulation 9A reduction` 2480 1000 7680 EQUALS 2480
